WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.734 --> 00:00:03.202
 Josh, Ben, congratulations.

00:00:03.269 --> 00:00:05.105
You guys have made
it to the final round

00:00:05.205 --> 00:00:06.305
of this competition.

00:00:06.405 --> 00:00:07.774
Now we're sending
you back to your home

00:00:07.874 --> 00:00:09.742
forge just to recreate
this iconic weapon

00:00:09.842 --> 00:00:14.147
from history, the ram dao.

00:00:18.184 --> 00:00:19.952
The ram-dao was a
sacrificial sword

00:00:20.019 --> 00:00:22.021
that descends from
the weapons of India's

00:00:22.121 --> 00:00:23.790
legendary Rajput warriors.

00:00:23.890 --> 00:00:26.992
It's broad, heavy blade flares
to an axe-like projection,

00:00:27.059 --> 00:00:28.428
which is ideally
suited to the ritual

00:00:28.494 --> 00:00:32.532
beheading of large animals
such as buffalo and goats.

00:00:32.598 --> 00:00:35.101
These sacrifices were made to
the Hindu goddess of death,

00:00:35.168 --> 00:00:37.103
Kali, whose symbolic
eye is often

00:00:37.203 --> 00:00:39.204
etched on the flared
end of the blade

00:00:39.305 --> 00:00:41.240
so she can watch
over the ceremony.

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:44.043
The eye of Kali can be
seen on the ram-dao wielded

00:00:44.110 --> 00:00:48.715
by Zodd in the comic
series "Berserk."

00:00:48.781 --> 00:00:52.552
Josh, Ben, your final challenge
is to forge a ram-dao.

00:00:52.652 --> 00:00:55.555
It must be an effective and
deadly version of the weapon

00:00:55.621 --> 00:00:57.123
that you see here.

00:00:57.190 --> 00:00:58.824
Just make sure that your blades
fall within the following

00:00:58.891 --> 00:01:00.092
parameters.

00:01:00.159 --> 00:01:01.894
The length of the blade
must be between 20

00:01:01.961 --> 00:01:03.529
and 23 inches in length.

00:01:03.596 --> 00:01:06.299
It must have a finial ball,
a decorative eye of Kali

00:01:06.399 --> 00:01:10.036
a demon buffalo head as
well as a disc pommel.

00:01:10.136 --> 00:01:11.637
Failure to meet a single
one of our parameters

00:01:11.738 --> 00:01:14.507
is grounds for immediate
dismissal from this forge,

00:01:14.574 --> 00:01:16.943
with no deliberation.

00:01:17.009 --> 00:01:19.011
 I feel excited
about it, because it's

00:01:19.111 --> 00:01:22.481
something that I've
never, ever done before.

00:01:22.582 --> 00:01:25.318
So let's do it.

00:01:25.384 --> 00:01:26.786
 You'll have four days
at your home forges

00:01:26.853 --> 00:01:28.454
in which to complete
this challenge.

00:01:28.554 --> 00:01:30.924
At the end of those four days,
you'll return and present

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:32.992
your weapons to our
panel of expert judges

00:01:33.092 --> 00:01:34.627
and after they've
thoroughly tested them,

00:01:34.694 --> 00:01:36.428
they'll declare one of
you the "Forged in Fire"

00:01:36.495 --> 00:01:39.765
champion who walks out of here
with a check for 10 grand.

00:01:39.865 --> 00:01:40.899
Good luck, bladesmiths.

00:01:40.966 --> 00:01:42.102
We'll see you in four days.

00:01:48.274 --> 00:01:50.243
 First thing I'm
trying to do is

00:01:50.310 --> 00:01:52.645
have a very, very
good visual of what

00:01:52.712 --> 00:01:54.147
I'm going to be aiming for.

00:01:54.214 --> 00:01:57.449
Also, we need to concentrate
on the finial right here.

00:01:57.549 --> 00:01:59.786
That's going to be something
that I need to keep my eye on,

00:01:59.853 --> 00:02:01.453
and it's going to
be a challenge.

00:02:01.553 --> 00:02:03.089
So this is the piece
I'm going to be using.

00:02:03.156 --> 00:02:05.724
It's 5160 steel.

00:02:05.791 --> 00:02:07.860
JOSH (VOICEOVER): I've never
really have shaped something

00:02:07.927 --> 00:02:10.963
like this before, so I feel
that the easiest way for me

00:02:11.030 --> 00:02:14.066
to shape that curve
is just to start

00:02:14.133 --> 00:02:16.068
using the anvil as a hammer.

00:02:16.168 --> 00:02:18.237
And it actually worked.

00:02:18.303 --> 00:02:20.239
First it's going great so far.

00:02:20.306 --> 00:02:22.976
We've got the
basic profile done.

00:02:23.042 --> 00:02:25.678
Then when it's over,
let's go have dinner.

00:02:25.745 --> 00:02:29.916
This is mi abuelita, the
matriarch of the family.

00:02:29.982 --> 00:02:33.586
I'm tired, and I'm ready to
stuff my face up with dinner.

00:02:33.686 --> 00:02:37.923 line:7%
 [speaking spanish]

00:02:38.023 --> 00:02:39.091
BEN: I'm back in my home forge.

00:02:39.158 --> 00:02:41.661
It is about five
degrees right now.

00:02:41.761 --> 00:02:44.363
Spring steel's a great material
for something like this that's

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:46.699
going to take a lot of
abuse and be able to flex

00:02:46.766 --> 00:02:48.301
over and over again.

00:02:48.368 --> 00:02:50.369
So what I'm going to try and do
first is drawing out the tang.

00:02:50.436 --> 00:02:51.971
I'm going to do a
through tang, so it's

00:02:52.038 --> 00:02:53.606
going to need to
be long, but also

00:02:53.673 --> 00:02:55.975
thicker than the rest of the
blade to give it strength.

00:02:56.075 --> 00:02:59.646
It's a big piece of
steel, but I'll cut it.

00:02:59.712 --> 00:03:02.614
Oh, here it goes.

00:03:02.681 --> 00:03:03.917
Boom.

00:03:04.017 --> 00:03:05.451
The sun is setting.

00:03:05.518 --> 00:03:07.453
It's starting to get even
colder than it already was,

00:03:07.519 --> 00:03:10.323
so I'm about to probably
call it a night.

00:03:13.926 --> 00:03:17.697
JOSH (VOICEOVER): All right, so
everything ready for quenching.

00:03:21.534 --> 00:03:25.772
The heat treatment is
the soul of the knife.

00:03:25.872 --> 00:03:27.273
This has to go well.

00:03:27.373 --> 00:03:31.811
And I'm just noticing
a slight curve.

00:03:31.911 --> 00:03:33.245
It's not going away.

00:03:33.345 --> 00:03:35.281
I'm not going to lose
because of a warp.

00:03:35.381 --> 00:03:37.183
I'm going to go
ahead and re-quench.

00:03:37.250 --> 00:03:40.086
If it doesn't go well, a
couple of things can happen.

00:03:40.153 --> 00:03:44.190
A big warp, or the worst
thing can be a crack.

00:03:44.257 --> 00:03:46.593
That's going to push me
to start all over again.

00:03:50.930 --> 00:03:54.033
Hopefully it worked.

00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:55.435
Yeah, yeah, beautiful.

00:03:58.738 --> 00:03:59.705
BEN: I have it hot-cut.

00:03:59.772 --> 00:04:02.174
Now I need to add the
sweep to it, which

00:04:02.241 --> 00:04:05.011
is going to be challenging.

00:04:05.111 --> 00:04:09.715
I almost forgot about the
decorative finial at the top.

00:04:09.815 --> 00:04:11.818
That's kind of one of
the things of being

00:04:11.884 --> 00:04:13.853
a ceremonial sacrificial sword.

00:04:13.919 --> 00:04:16.688
There's a lot of stuff on it
that's decorative that serves

00:04:16.755 --> 00:04:19.058
no purpose other than
for religious use,

00:04:19.125 --> 00:04:23.429
but I forget about it because
I'm used to making this stuff.

00:04:23.496 --> 00:04:25.731
OK, the blade looks good.

00:04:25.831 --> 00:04:27.433
I've got enough
material to work with,

00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:31.938
so I'm going to go take it
downstairs, start grinding.

00:04:32.038 --> 00:04:35.741
This is my homemade
belt grinder,

00:04:35.841 --> 00:04:37.543
and this is how I have
to start this thing.

00:04:37.643 --> 00:04:39.812
[grinding]

00:04:47.053 --> 00:04:48.053
It's straight.

00:04:48.120 --> 00:04:50.022
I have my bevels ground in.

00:04:50.122 --> 00:04:52.257
It is the shape it needs to be.

00:04:52.324 --> 00:04:55.494 line:0%
I'm looking to
heat treat tonight.

00:04:55.561 --> 00:04:57.463 line:7%
 Start of day four is here.

00:04:57.530 --> 00:05:00.499
I'm going to go ahead and
start working on the handle.

00:05:00.599 --> 00:05:02.835
Ideally what I want,
is to have a handle--

00:05:02.902 --> 00:05:05.304
not just nice-looking,
beautiful, but also is

00:05:05.404 --> 00:05:07.873
something that is comfortable.

00:05:07.974 --> 00:05:10.676
So I need to have a handle
that has a grip to it,

00:05:10.742 --> 00:05:16.081
that it doesn't feel like it's
going to fly off the hands.

00:05:16.148 --> 00:05:18.451
I've never done a finial.

00:05:18.518 --> 00:05:20.786
This was definitely
very challenging.

00:05:20.886 --> 00:05:25.257
I went with a
diamond-looking piece.

00:05:25.324 --> 00:05:27.426
It's different.

00:05:27.493 --> 00:05:29.795
I need to really
make this blade pop,

00:05:29.895 --> 00:05:32.799
so besides the eye in
the crown, I decide

00:05:32.899 --> 00:05:34.767
to add extra edging to it.

00:05:34.834 --> 00:05:37.070 line:0%
But no matter how
beautiful the blade

00:05:37.170 --> 00:05:41.040 line:0%
is, if you miss one
of the parameters,

00:05:41.106 --> 00:05:43.942 line:7%
you're out of the competition.

00:05:44.042 --> 00:05:45.478 line:7%
BEN (VOICEOVER): It's day four.

00:05:45.544 --> 00:05:48.313
There's a bit of a
warp that happened

00:05:48.380 --> 00:05:50.916
during the tempering
of the spine,

00:05:50.983 --> 00:05:52.685
and I don't have enough
time to re-quench.

00:05:52.752 --> 00:05:55.387
I have too much
other stuff to do,

00:05:55.454 --> 00:05:59.558
but I can still make
this blade look the part.

00:05:59.658 --> 00:06:01.526
I can still make it perform
really, really, well,

00:06:01.593 --> 00:06:03.329
so that's my goal for today.

00:06:03.429 --> 00:06:05.865
[grinding]

00:06:09.835 --> 00:06:12.038
[hammering]

00:06:14.607 --> 00:06:16.976
I'm just getting to
work on the finial.

00:06:17.076 --> 00:06:19.378
It doesn't have to look
like anything in particular,

00:06:19.444 --> 00:06:21.680
it's just kind of
a knob at the end.

00:06:21.780 --> 00:06:23.582
I don't do a whole
lot of engraving,

00:06:23.682 --> 00:06:26.919
so this is kind of out
of my comfort zone.

00:06:26.985 --> 00:06:30.422
But after some light sanding,
it's going to be done.

00:06:30.523 --> 00:06:34.193
So I'm ready to
go cut something.

00:06:34.293 --> 00:06:35.695
Whoo.

00:06:35.762 --> 00:06:36.862
That's sharp.

00:06:36.929 --> 00:06:40.365
 All right, bladesmiths,
welcome to the kill test.

00:06:40.432 --> 00:06:44.469
Ram-dao, ram carcass.

00:06:44.536 --> 00:06:45.371
Josh, you're up first.

00:06:45.471 --> 00:06:46.939
You ready for this?

00:06:47.006 --> 00:06:47.907
 Well, let's kill it again.

00:06:50.510 --> 00:06:54.246
Doug is holding my ram-dao
and I'm just thinking,

00:06:54.313 --> 00:06:55.381
just chop the head off.

00:06:55.448 --> 00:06:56.749
Just chop it.

00:06:56.849 --> 00:07:00.252
My heart is just pumping
10,000 miles per hour, man.

00:07:00.319 --> 00:07:02.088
[music playing]

00:07:07.860 --> 00:07:08.728
 Oh, my god.

00:07:08.828 --> 00:07:11.097
[slashing]

00:07:17.436 --> 00:07:20.573
 Oh, my god.

00:07:20.673 --> 00:07:23.075
[laughs]

00:07:23.175 --> 00:07:25.477
 All right, Josh, let's
talk about your ram-dao here.

00:07:25.578 --> 00:07:27.479
The blade you have
here is sharp.

00:07:27.579 --> 00:07:31.117
For every pass it
makes, it cuts deeply.

00:07:31.183 --> 00:07:34.954
But I also love what you
have in the sense of balance.

00:07:35.054 --> 00:07:36.889
That even though it's
a chopper, the recovery

00:07:36.989 --> 00:07:39.224
is just comfortable
enough to where you

00:07:39.324 --> 00:07:40.960
can cut all the way through.

00:07:41.027 --> 00:07:42.361
It feels good in the hand.

00:07:42.428 --> 00:07:45.364
It's got a great balance, and
most importantly, it will kill.

00:07:45.431 --> 00:07:46.298
Good job.

00:07:46.365 --> 00:07:47.166
 That's awesome.

00:07:47.266 --> 00:07:48.567
Thank you.

00:07:48.667 --> 00:07:49.869
 All right, Ben,
it's your turn.

00:07:49.936 --> 00:07:50.736
You ready for this?

00:07:50.837 --> 00:07:51.269
 I'm excited.

00:07:51.336 --> 00:07:53.572
Let's do it.

00:07:53.639 --> 00:07:55.073
BEN: Right now,
I'm really excited.

00:07:55.173 --> 00:07:56.541
I've put my best work into this.

00:07:56.608 --> 00:07:58.877
Nothing's perfect,
but my biggest concern

00:07:58.944 --> 00:08:01.180
is that there was a
slight warp that I

00:08:01.246 --> 00:08:02.514
just really couldn't get out.

00:08:02.581 --> 00:08:05.417
So I'm really hoping
that my blade outperforms

00:08:05.517 --> 00:08:07.653
Josh's in every other
way so that it's

00:08:07.720 --> 00:08:10.655
a flaw can be overlooked.

00:08:10.756 --> 00:08:15.160
 Something's off
about this design.

00:08:15.227 --> 00:08:16.128
 There's a bit of an issue.

00:08:19.999 --> 00:08:22.334
BEN (VOICEOVER): At this
point, I'm a bit confused.

00:08:22.400 --> 00:08:23.503
I don't know what's going on.

00:08:30.409 --> 00:08:32.978
 Ben, your blade doesn't
have a finial bowl.

00:08:33.078 --> 00:08:36.148
One of the defining
characteristics of the ram-dao.

00:08:36.249 --> 00:08:37.716
It was also one
of the parameters,

00:08:37.816 --> 00:08:40.419
and the judges feel that
your blade cannot be tested

00:08:40.519 --> 00:08:42.588
evenly and fairly with Josh's.

00:08:42.688 --> 00:08:44.857
Dave Baker is going
to tell you why.

00:08:44.924 --> 00:08:46.658
 The design of the
ram-dao has that

00:08:46.758 --> 00:08:48.160
finial at the end of a blade.

00:08:48.227 --> 00:08:50.229
That finial can wind up
being a cut restrictor,

00:08:50.296 --> 00:08:52.498
not allowing the blade
to pass through a target.

00:08:52.565 --> 00:08:55.233
It also keeps that blade
from being able to stab.

00:08:55.300 --> 00:08:56.701
Yours doesn't have that.

00:08:56.768 --> 00:08:58.537
How can we test them evenly?

00:08:58.603 --> 00:08:59.538
BEN: I understand.

00:08:59.605 --> 00:09:00.973
 Ben, "Forged in
Fire" champions

00:09:01.040 --> 00:09:02.375
don't miss parameters.

00:09:02.441 --> 00:09:04.343
I'd like to invite you
to shake our hands,

00:09:04.443 --> 00:09:06.244
shake your competitor's
hand, and then

00:09:06.311 --> 00:09:07.079
please leave the forge.

00:09:11.117 --> 00:09:12.351 line:7%
 I'm pretty disappointed.

00:09:12.418 --> 00:09:15.320
I really wanted to see my
blade chop through that ram.

00:09:15.387 --> 00:09:19.425
But I'm happy with what I turned
in, and at the end of the day,

00:09:19.491 --> 00:09:20.692
I think I'm definitely
leaving a better

00:09:20.792 --> 00:09:22.228
bladesmith than when I came in.

00:09:25.564 --> 00:09:26.865
 Josh, congratulations.

00:09:26.965 --> 00:09:28.634
You're the "Forged
in Fire" champion,

00:09:28.701 --> 00:09:31.002
and that's a title that comes
with a check for $10,000.

00:09:31.069 --> 00:09:33.739
Come on forward and
shake our hands, brother.

00:09:33.839 --> 00:09:36.041
 I cannot believe
this is happening.

00:09:36.141 --> 00:09:38.844
I think what I'm going to do
with the $10,000 is going to go

00:09:38.911 --> 00:09:42.247
to open a shop where I'm
going to be providing

00:09:42.314 --> 00:09:45.551
workshops for at-risk youth.

00:09:45.617 --> 00:09:49.654
My abuelita told me
go, win, and come back.

00:09:49.721 --> 00:09:50.388
Mission accomplished.

00:09:50.489 --> 00:09:53.192
[music playing]

